1. What you can do

  a) Play with the Mod, on your own or on a server, including servers that earn money, as long as you follow the
     Minecraft EULA.

  b) Include the Mod in modpacks, public or private, free or monetized, when the pack is distributed through
     CurseForge or Modrinth (or another platform that downloads the Mod from its official pages), following that
     platform's rules.

  c) Make content for the Mod: datapacks, resource packs, configs, scripts and similar files, and share or sell them
     however you like. These are your own work.

  d) Make addon or compatibility mods that use the Mod's public API, if it has one, as a dependency, without copying
     the Mod's code into them.

  e) Copy, change and redistribute any files the Mod's documentation marks as examples or templates (such as example
     datapacks), for any purpose, without credit.

  f) Read the source code to learn from it, and to write compatibility or addon code against it.

  g) Show the Mod in videos, streams, screenshots, reviews and articles, monetized or not.


2. What you can't do without written permission

  a) Redistribute the Mod's files, original or modified, anywhere other than the Mod's official pages (such as its
     CurseForge, Modrinth or source repository pages). Link to those pages instead of re-uploading.

  b) Make or distribute forks, ports (to another mod loader, Minecraft version or platform) or rewrites of the Mod, or
     other works based on its code or assets.

  c) Copy the Mod's code or assets, in full or in substantial parts, into another project.

  d) Use the Mod's code, assets or documentation as training, fine-tuning or evaluation data for artificial
     intelligence or machine learning models, or include them in datasets made for that purpose.

  e) Use AI tools to produce ports, rewrites, translations to another language or loader, or other derivative works of
     the Mod, or distribute such works. This applies whether or not any of the Mod's code is copied directly.

  f) Claim the Mod, or any part of it, as your own work.


